<section class="section product-faq"><div class="section-kicker">PRODUCT &amp; AI FAQ <span>08 / 05</span></div><h2>Clear answers.<br><em>Practical choices.</em></h2><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>Do I need AI to use ProcessArc?</summary><p>No. The process registry, ownership, workflow, cycle-time and optimization features are useful without any model connection.</p></details><details><summary>Where is my data stored?</summary><p>The demo stores sample records in its configured SQL database. For a deployment, storage location and retention depend on the environment selected by the organization operating the service. The public CSV analyzer does not retain uploaded files.</p></details><details><summary>Can I use my own model?</summary><p>The application supports a configurable Ollama endpoint for local Qwen models. The analyzer can optionally be configured to use an OpenAI-compatible NVIDIA NIM endpoint, with local or rules-based fallbacks.</p></details><details><summary>Is NVIDIA currently integrated?</summary><p>The NVIDIA technologies on this page are proposed options. Only successful calls to a configured NVIDIA NIM endpoint for the Process Insight Analyzer will be labelled as built with NIM for that tool.</p></details></div></section>
